# Tailwind CSS v4 — CSS-First Configuration

This project uses Tailwind v4 with CSS-first configuration. There is **no `tailwind.config.ts`** — do not create one.

All theme tokens are defined in `app/globals.css`:

- `@theme inline { ... }` block maps CSS variables to Tailwind utilities.
- `:root` and `.dark` define color values in **OKLCH** color space.
- Dark mode: `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *))` with class strategy via next-themes.

## Design Tokens

```tsx
// ✅ Semantic tokens — auto-switch in dark mode
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border" />
<div className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground" />
<div className="text-muted-foreground" />

// ❌ Hardcoded — breaks dark mode and design consistency
<div className="bg-white text-black" />
<div className="bg-[#1a1a1a]" />
```

## Adding New Tokens

1. Add CSS variables in `:root` and `.dark` blocks in `globals.css` (OKLCH values).
2. Map in `@theme inline`: `--color-my-token: var(--my-token);`
3. Use as Tailwind utilities: `bg-my-token`, `text-my-token`.
